{
  "statement": "The requirements I propose focus on enhancing the sustainability of the ATM system. GRN-01 aims to minimize energy consumption during transaction processing, which is crucial for reducing operational costs and environmental impact. GRN-02 provides transparency by reporting the carbon footprint of each transaction, promoting awareness. GRN-03 ensures the use of energy-efficient hardware, reducing overall energy usage. GRN-04 minimizes data storage requirements, which contributes to lower energy consumption. GRN-05 offers clients electronic transaction records, reducing paper waste. GRN-06 promotes energy savings by shutting down during inactivity. GRN-07 ensures annual assessments of environmental impact, fostering continuous improvement in sustainability practices.",
  "conflicts_raised": [
    {
      "ids": ["GRN-01", "EFF-01"],
      "type": "resource",
      "description": "GRN-01's focus on minimizing energy consumption may conflict with EFF-01's requirement for processing transactions within 3 seconds, potentially increasing energy use."
    },
    {
      "ids": ["GRN-02", "TRU-03"],
      "type": "redundant",
      "description": "GRN-02's carbon footprint report may overlap with TRU-03's logging requirements, as both involve tracking transaction details."
    }
  ],
